{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a stitch task (task #5434) from a work queue in the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd065-factor requirements R3.1-R3.4 for the `cmd/factor` utility. Specifically:\n   - R3.1: When --help is the first argument, print usage to stdout and exit 0\n   - R3.2: When --version is the first argument, print version info to stdout and exit 0\n   - R3.3: Write factorization output to stdout, one line per integer\n   - R3.4: Write error messages to stderr without stopping processing of remaining inputs\n   \n   The task requires modifying `cmd/factor/main.go` and `cmd/factor/factor_test.go`, following the differential testing pattern, and verifying acceptance criteria (go build, go vet, go test all pass).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU `gfactor`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Trial division prime factorization for int64 range\n   - GNU factor output format: `NUMBER: FACTOR FACTOR ...`\n   - Binary name normalization in tests using regex replacement\n   - The execution constitution mandates: no git commands, write all code before building, 40-line function limit, copyright headers, etc.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd065-factor.yaml`\n     - Contains the full SRD specification for factor utility\n     - R3 group (the target requirements): R3.1 (--help), R3.2 (--version), R3.3 (stdout output), R3.4 (stderr errors with continued processing)\n     - Important: R3.3 and R3.4 appear to already be satisfied by existing code\n\n   - `cmd/factor/main.go` (existing, 121 lines)\n     - Already has --help and --version handling in main() lines 29-38\n     - Already writes to stdout (fmt.Println in printFactors)\n     - Already writes errors to stderr (fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...) in processArgs and processStdin)\n     - Already continues processing after errors\n     - Key existing code:\n     ```go\n     const helpText = `Usage: factor [NUMBER]...\n     Print the prime factors of each specified integer.\n     `\n     const versionText = `factor (go-unix-utils) 0.1.0`\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n             switch os.Args[1] {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Print(helpText)\n                 return\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Println(versionText)\n                 return\n             }\n         }\n         exitCode := 0\n         if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n             exitCode = processArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         } else {\n             exitCode = processStdin()\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     ```\n     - Functions: `processArgs`, `processStdin`, `factorize`, `primeFactors`, `printFactors`\n\n   - `cmd/factor/factor_test.go` (existing, 101 lines)\n     - Has TestDiff with 16 test cases covering R1 and R2 requirements\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gfactor\")`\n     - Has binary name normalization regex for error message comparison\n     - Does NOT have test cases for --help or --version flags\n     - Key test structure:\n     ```go\n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gfactor\")\n         if err != nil {\n             t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n         }\n         binaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?factor`)\n         normalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n             return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"factor\"))\n         })\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{...}\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - the task was interrupted after reading files but before implementation began.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R3.3 (stdout output) and R3.4 (stderr errors with continued processing) are already implemented in the existing code from R1/R2 requirement groups.\n   - R3.1 (--help) and R3.2 (--version) are also already implemented in main.go, but lack test coverage.\n   - The main work needed is: adding differential test cases for --help and --version, and potentially adjusting the help/version output format to match GNU gfactor exactly.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive user message containing the full stitch task specification with: role definition, repository_files listing, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/factor/main.go` to ensure R3.1-R3.4 compliance (may already be compliant; needs verification against gfactor output format)\n   - Add differential test cases for --help and --version to `cmd/factor/factor_test.go`\n   - Update the spec comment at top of main.go to include R3.1-R3.4\n   - Run `go build -o bin/factor ./cmd/factor/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/factor/...` to verify no issues (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/factor/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass (AC3)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, factor_test.go) and was about to begin planning and implementing. The existing code already appears to handle R3.1-R3.4 functionality, so the main work is:\n   1. Adding --help and --version test cases to the test file\n   2. Updating the package doc comment to reference R3.1-R3.4\n   3. Potentially adjusting help/version output to match gfactor's exact format\n   4. Running build, vet, and test to verify acceptance criteria\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the changes: First, modify `cmd/factor/main.go` to update the spec comment to include R3.1-R3.4. Then add differential test cases for `--help` and `--version` to `cmd/factor/factor_test.go`. The --help/--version tests need normalization since gfactor's help/version text will differ from our implementation. Then run build, vet, and test commands to verify all acceptance criteria pass. The task description states: \"Add functionality for srd065-factor requirements R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4\" and \"Add differential test cases covering R3.1-R3.4\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5434/7918ac6d-1ed0-4119-821d-71202c4a58b4.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7918ac6d-1ed0-4119-821d-71202c4a58b4","uuid":"a3b3e27f-78e7-46df-8097-56b4f2bfcbd9","timestamp":"2026-05-21T18:32:07.253Z","isSynthetic":true}
