{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TocwPXpxjc5iszbvzeSrwi","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a good set of examples. Let me compile the findings.\n\n## Summary\n\nI found 3-4 excellent examples of how cmd/ utilities test --help and --version flags using the `testutils.DiffTest` differential testing pattern. Here are the key examples:\n\n### Example 1: **pwd** (cmd/pwd/pwd_test.go, lines 109-121)\n\nThis is a clean pattern where --help and --version outputs are discarded because the text differs from the reference binary:\n\n```go\n// --help and --version (discard stdout since text differs)\n{\n\tName:      \"help\",\n\tArgs:      []string{\"--help\"},\n\tEnv:       lcEnv,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n{\n\tName:      \"version\",\n\tArgs:      []string{\"--version\"},\n\tEnv:       lcEnv,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n```\n\nThe key insight is the use of a `NormalizeFunc` that discards stdout (`discardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })`). This allows testing that the flag is recognized and exits cleanly without comparing the actual help/version text output.\n\n### Example 2: **true** (cmd/true/true_test.go, lines 31-41)\n\nSimilar pattern, testing that --help and --version work but exit with code 0:\n\n```go\n{\n\tName:     \"help\",\n\tArgs:     []string{\"--help\"},\n\tExitCode: 0,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n{\n\tName:     \"version\",\n\tArgs:     []string{\"--version\"},\n\tExitCode: 0,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n```\n\n### Example 3: **whoami** (cmd/whoami/whoami_test.go, lines 30-36)\n\nNotably, whoami's test does *not* include --help or --version tests in its DiffTest suite:\n\n```go\ntests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t{Name: \"no_args\", ExitCode: 0},\n\t{Name: \"extra_operand\", Args: []string{\"extraarg\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n\t{Name: \"unknown_flag\", Args: []string{\"--unknown\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n}\n```\n\nThis shows that not all utilities test these flags with DiffTest—it depends on whether the utility supports them.\n\n### Key Pattern Summary\n\nThe differential testing pattern for --help and --version relies on:\n1. Creating a `testutils.DiffTest` entry with `Args: []string{\"--help\"}` or `Args: []string{\"--version\"}`\n2. Using `Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout}` to normalize away the actual output text (since implementations differ)\n3. Optionally specifying `ExitCode` to verify expected exit codes\n4. Setting environment variables like `Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}` for consistency\n\nFiles examined:\n- /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5434/cmd/pwd/pwd_test.go\n- /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5434/cmd/true/true_test.go\n- /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5434/cmd/whoami/whoami_test.go"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7918ac6d-1ed0-4119-821d-71202c4a58b4","uuid":"8196c5f2-49fb-45c2-838c-c97688011ff0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T18:32:38.883Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5434, find examples of how other cmd/ utilities test --help and --version flags in their *_test.go files using the differential testing pattern (testutils.DiffTest). Show me 2-3 examples of the test case definitions. Search breadth: medium.","agentId":"a4c30a20da816d867","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a good set of examples. Let me compile the findings.\n\n## Summary\n\nI found 3-4 excellent examples of how cmd/ utilities test --help and --version flags using the `testutils.DiffTest` differential testing pattern. Here are the key examples:\n\n### Example 1: **pwd** (cmd/pwd/pwd_test.go, lines 109-121)\n\nThis is a clean pattern where --help and --version outputs are discarded because the text differs from the reference binary:\n\n```go\n// --help and --version (discard stdout since text differs)\n{\n\tName:      \"help\",\n\tArgs:      []string{\"--help\"},\n\tEnv:       lcEnv,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n{\n\tName:      \"version\",\n\tArgs:      []string{\"--version\"},\n\tEnv:       lcEnv,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n```\n\nThe key insight is the use of a `NormalizeFunc` that discards stdout (`discardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })`). This allows testing that the flag is recognized and exits cleanly without comparing the actual help/version text output.\n\n### Example 2: **true** (cmd/true/true_test.go, lines 31-41)\n\nSimilar pattern, testing that --help and --version work but exit with code 0:\n\n```go\n{\n\tName:     \"help\",\n\tArgs:     []string{\"--help\"},\n\tExitCode: 0,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n{\n\tName:     \"version\",\n\tArgs:     []string{\"--version\"},\n\tExitCode: 0,\n\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout},\n},\n```\n\n### Example 3: **whoami** (cmd/whoami/whoami_test.go, lines 30-36)\n\nNotably, whoami's test does *not* include --help or --version tests in its DiffTest suite:\n\n```go\ntests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t{Name: \"no_args\", ExitCode: 0},\n\t{Name: \"extra_operand\", Args: []string{\"extraarg\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n\t{Name: \"unknown_flag\", Args: []string{\"--unknown\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n}\n```\n\nThis shows that not all utilities test these flags with DiffTest—it depends on whether the utility supports them.\n\n### Key Pattern Summary\n\nThe differential testing pattern for --help and --version relies on:\n1. Creating a `testutils.DiffTest` entry with `Args: []string{\"--help\"}` or `Args: []string{\"--version\"}`\n2. Using `Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStdout}` to normalize away the actual output text (since implementations differ)\n3. Optionally specifying `ExitCode` to verify expected exit codes\n4. Setting environment variables like `Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}` for consistency\n\nFiles examined:\n- /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5434/cmd/pwd/pwd_test.go\n- /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5434/cmd/true/true_test.go\n- /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5434/cmd/whoami/whoami_test.go"}],"totalDurationMs":20543,"totalTokens":36692,"totalToolUseCount":8,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1558,"cache_read_input_tokens":34175,"output_tokens":953,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1558},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":34175,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1558,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":5,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
